%[text] %[text:anchor:T_534a] # Separation of Variables 
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:MainMenu.m)
%[text] When solving first-order ordinary differential equations, a good first approach is check whether the equation is separable. This is because **separation of variables** is typically the most straightforward analytical method to solve a differential equation. In this script, we'll learn and practice how to use this method, using an application of logistic population growth to help us do so.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"} %[text:anchor:M_597CA885]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_51183E7B] **Before you get started:**
